  "title": "hpke case",
  "description": "RFC 9180 HPKE, mode Base, X25519/HKDF-SHA256/AES-256-GCM. `sealSequence`: one sender context with a fixed ephemeral key, messages sealed in order. `open`: single-shot open. 04 \u00a73.3 (G-46, D-66): `deriveFromCek`: the `agentlink/v1/cek-eph` derivation ikm_j (HKDF-SHA256, ikm = CEK, empty salt, info = utf8(label) || raw 16-byte id || raw 32-byte recipient key), or a refusal; `recipientPublicKey` is absent when the case tests its absence. `wrapCek`: the CEK wrap with skE_j = ikm_j as the raw X25519 secret key (no DeriveKeyPair), info = utf8(\"agentlink/v1/cek\") || raw 16-byte id, empty AAD. `wrapCekWithEphemeralKey`: the same seal with the ephemeral secret given (the explicit-ephemeral path). `unwrapCek`: open one entry. `checkWrap`: recompute the entry from the public key and the CEK and compare the bytes. enc and wk are base64url without padding.",
